WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.802
-Our next guest
is a very funny comedian

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.404
whose stand-up special
"Good Clean Filth"

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.306
is streaming now on HBO Max.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.740
Let's take a look.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.609
-I found the best way
to discourage something in bed

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:12.145
that you're not into
is to try to get them

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.714
to not be into it on their own,
you know?

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.482
Try to ruin it for them.

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.317
So, I gave in at first.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:21.454
It was hard, but I was like,
"Oh, yeah, does daddy like that?

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.322
What about this?
Does daddy like this?"

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:25.158
And by the end of it,
I was just like,

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:30.897
"Dada! Dada! Dada!
Dada! Dada! Dada! Pbht!"

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:34.167
-Please welcome back to the show
Nikki Glaser, everybody!

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.235
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:41.808 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:47.380 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.482
Hi, Nikki! How are you?

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.184
-I'm so good, Seth Meyers.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:54.286
-You look wonderful, as always.
-Thank you. I forgot a bra.

00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:56.189
-Oh, well.
-Aw. Sometimes happens.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.556
-Sometimes that's how it goes.

00:00:57.556 --> 00:00:59.258
-You know what I realized?
-What's that?

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:01.594
-I look like you.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.062
-Ohh.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:05.431
-I have makeup on, but that's
really the only difference

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:06.866
between our faces.
-Yeah.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.902
-We have the same face,
and it's --

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.837
I am flattered
that I look like you.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:13.706
I'm complimenting myself,
and I'm not insulting you.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.042
-Well, I've always found you
very attractive,

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.610
so this makes sense now.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.946
-That's so -- [ Laughs ]

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.915
Like a true narcissist.
Exactly. Like, yes.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:24.751
No, I realize, though,

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.219
that most women's faces
without makeup just do look --

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:29.622
You can pretty much
pair them with a guy

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:33.192
because guys are just --
We have the same faces.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.828
For instance, if I was to ask
the audience to, like,

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.863
draw a picture of a smiley face

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:40.800
and I go, "Now make it a woman,"
what would you do?

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.735
You wouldn't, like,
scribble a vagina.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.804
Like, no one even knows
how to draw one of those.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.772
You wouldn't, like,
make it holding less money.

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:50.176
You would just add eyelashes.
It's what sets...

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.945
women and men apart is makeup,
so thank God for it.

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:54.113
But do you know
who we look like?

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:55.581
And this I was hurt by.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:58.151
-This is late breaking news.
You brought a photo.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.152
-I just came up with it
backstage because I go,

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:01.520
"Oh, my God,"

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.157
because someone told me
I look like this duo.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:07.126
But now I go, "I got a partner,
and now we look like this duo."

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:10.663
We look like the Nelson brothers
from Nelson.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.832
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.769
Get up here with me.
-Yeah, there we go.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.905
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.639
Yeah.
-I mean, look at us.

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:23.143
Look at that.
-There you go.

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:25.744
-It's -- It's spooky.
And I like it.

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:27.313
So thanks for sharing it
with me.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.748
-I mean, I've always been
a fan of theirs, too.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.149
This is all coming together.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:32.218
-Do you ever -- Have you ever
put on makeup?

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.887
Have you ever like --
Sometimes I see a guy's face

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.988
and I'm like, "I just want to
get a little eyeliner in there."

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:39.391
-I remember I played
one of the cast members

00:02:39.391 --> 00:02:42.962
in a "Desperate Housewives"
sketch in "SNL" back in the day.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.097
-Yes.
-I looked great, yeah.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.364
-You would!

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:48.600
It's amazing what it does.
It's, um --

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.638
I spray tan my body constantly.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:54.439
Like, my regular pallor
is probably like

00:02:54.439 --> 00:02:56.942
a Uncle Fester-ish color,

00:02:56.942 --> 00:02:59.345
and when people recognize me
without makeup,

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.780
I honestly get offended.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.548
I go,
"You think I look like this?"

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:04.750
'Cause I spray paint my body.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:08.154 line:0%
I use Sally Hansen leg spray.
This is all painted on.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.589 line:0%
It's all gonna --
My shower is gonna look like

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:13.492 line:0%
the water in Flint, Michigan,
when I bathe later.

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:16.295
That is not an insult.
It's a problem. Let's fix it.

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:18.530
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:21.133
-It is. Let's fix it.
-Yeah, that's still happening.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.702
It's a nice reminder of it
in that joke

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.970
that I made fun of them.
-We were talking backstage.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.639
You moved back
to your hometown...

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.107
-Of St. Louis.
-...of St. Louis at the

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.742
beginning of the pandemic,
and then it took.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.078
-I was scared because
the world was shutting down

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:34.179
and I didn't have
comedy clubs and podcasts

00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:35.748
to fill my life with,
and so I was like,

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.116
"I need to go
to Mommy and Daddy."

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.651
And so I went back to St. Louis

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.019
for what I thought
would be like two weeks,

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.155
like we all did,
like, "Until this blows over."

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.490
And then I lived there
for 10 months

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.259
with my parents in their house
at the age of 35.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:49.295
I eventually had to move out
because it was getting

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.597
embarrassing to have people
ask me where I was living

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.332
and I'd say,
"I live with my parents,"

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:54.833
and they'd be like, "Why?"

00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:57.203
And so I got rid of that
therapist, and I was like,

00:03:57.203 --> 00:04:00.172
"I don't really want
to talk about that anymore.

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:01.641
Can we talk about
why I'm so talented?

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.309
Like, I loved
when we focused on that."

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.078
But I eventually moved out,

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.546
and then I got an apartment
and I lived there

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:08.781
and I had a reality show
based on me living there.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.149
-And St. Louis appreciates it.

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.985
They had Nikki Glaser Day,
April 28th.

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:15.020
-Yes. I think it was
just a one-time thing.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.223
-You don't think
it's gonna be every April 28th?

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.457
-Oh, I would love it so much,

00:04:18.457 --> 00:04:20.459
but it was --
it was Nikki Glaser Day.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:22.895
I, as a comedian,
absolutely love attention.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:25.864
But this just felt like --
I came up with it,

00:04:25.864 --> 00:04:28.301
so it felt so embarrassing.
It really was --

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:29.802
E!, the network
that my reality show,

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:32.938
"Welcome Home Nikki Glaser?" --
still streaming on Peacock...

00:04:32.938 --> 00:04:35.508
It was --
E! bought Nikki Glaser Day.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.510
You can buy a day in the city.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.611
And they gave me a proclamation
from the mayor.

00:04:39.611 --> 00:04:40.980
They gave me a key to the city.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.748
-Wow. Double key.
-Double key.

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:45.718
-Double-key guest day.
-I know! You're getting 'em all.

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:49.288
-And you threw out a first pitch
at a Cardinals game.

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:52.191
-Yes, at the Busch Stadium.
Threw out the first pitch.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:54.693
Which I did not want to do
because I'm not athletic at all.

00:04:54.693 --> 00:04:56.395
I got first voted off
"Dancing with the Stars."

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:58.264
It's like --
It's traumatic for me.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:04:59.598
-Yeah.
-But I accepted

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:01.067
because it's every --
It's, like, my boyfriend --

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.669
It's all my best guy friends'
Make-A-Wish to do this.

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:05.137
So they're like,
"You got to do it!"

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:10.042
So I did it, and I did not do
as well as I wanted.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:12.344
I will not watch the footage.
I don't know how it went.

00:05:12.344 --> 00:05:15.181
People keep sending it to me
as an abusive tactic.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.482
I block them.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:19.252
-Is that bad
that we have the footage?

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:20.953
-Do I -- Can I close my eyes
a little bit?

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.588
Can I watch it
like I watch "Saw"?

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:23.956
-I think -- Why don't --
Hey, wait.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.858
Why don't you
close your eyes completely

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.693
and then, just by
the audience reaction,

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:29.328
try to picture what it is?
-Okay.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:31.997
-You tell me if this
was as bad as 50 Cent...

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:33.732
-Okay. Here we go.
-...and his first pitch.

00:05:33.732 --> 00:05:35.935
-Here's Nikki's first pitch.
-Oh, God.

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:37.570
-Here comes the windup
and the pitch.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.904
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:40.739
Thank you, Nikki!

00:05:40.739 --> 00:05:43.309
-Do you see me? Ugh!

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:46.379
Oh. I was so sad.
I cried so much later on.

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:48.281
-No, you didn't.
-I -- Oh. Oh.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:50.115
-That was great!

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:51.684
-It was so bad.
It was so embarrassing.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.252
But the worst part
of that whole thing,

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.288
the catcher
that I was throwing --

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:57.389
that I tried
to throw the ball to

00:05:57.389 --> 00:05:59.625
was the guy who lived
in my apartment building.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.260
I flirted with him.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.929
I hit on him one day
by offering him a dog treat

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:06.164
in the lobby of our hotel --
or of my apartment building,

00:06:06.164 --> 00:06:08.367
which I thought would be funny
because I was offering --

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.036
I go, "Hey, you want
to a treat?" to my dog.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.470
And then I go,
"Do you want a treat?"

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.005
And then I thought
that was a good line.

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.840
We had a conversation
in the elevator.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.042
I then DM'd him to be like,
"Hey. Nice meeting you."

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:20.479
Never heard back. So then
I had to pitch the ball to --

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:22.248
This was my second pitch
to that guy.

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:25.918
And it -- That one was worse,
actually.

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:27.353
-He probably saw that pitch,

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.755
and he was like,
"The one that got away."

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.490
-[ Laughter ]
-Literally.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.192
-Yeah, exactly.
-He was like...

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:36.194
-So, wait. You have a wonderful
new stand-up special on Netflix.

00:06:36.194 --> 00:06:37.897
You have always been --
-No. HBO.

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:40.199
-Oh, excuse me. I'm so sorry.
Let me reboot it.

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:42.034
-I got one on Netflix, too,
but HBO.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.036
-Great.
Just dabble, everybody.

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:45.738
-Try them all. But HBO.
"Good Clean Filth."

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:47.740
-And the other one is --

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.575
And your reality show's
on Peacock.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.511
-And my reality show's
on Peacock,

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:53.045
and "FBoy Island" is on HBO Max.

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:54.613
-So you got a lot
of networks covered.

00:06:54.613 --> 00:06:56.248
-I got it all covered.

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:58.951
-But your new HBO
stand-up special,

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:01.120
you have always been really open
about talking about sex,

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.455
especially in a way
that we never get to talk

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:05.023
about in this society,
but I want to ask.

00:07:05.023 --> 00:07:06.559
Your parents --
Obviously you're close.

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:08.360
You went and stayed with them
during a pandemic.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:11.530
How do they feel about
watching a show like yours,

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.832
which is very open about things

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:14.599
that are usually
behind closed doors?

00:07:14.599 --> 00:07:16.768
-They are such supportive
parents, and I didn't realize

00:07:16.768 --> 00:07:18.570
that they hated it so much

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:21.706
until they were on my reality
show and I heard --

00:07:21.706 --> 00:07:22.842
You know those like --

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:24.143
where they do
the individual interviews

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:25.778
during reality shows
and you watch them and you go,

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:27.412
"Why would this person
be saying this stuff?

00:07:27.412 --> 00:07:30.216
Don't they know people are
gonna hear what they say?"

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:31.717
Like, my mom did that to me.

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:33.319
She was in an interview
and she was like,

00:07:33.319 --> 00:07:35.421
"You know what?
If she wasn't my daughter,

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:37.756
I wouldn't go to her shows.
I wouldn't be a fan."

00:07:37.756 --> 00:07:39.658
And I go, "Mom,
it's supposed to go --

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:41.493
Did you misspeak?
If I wasn't your daughter,

00:07:41.493 --> 00:07:43.162
maybe you could stomach
the stuff that I..."

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:46.065
She goes, "No, I would
hate it if -- I only go..."

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:48.234
I look at everyone and I go,

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:50.702
"I can't believe
all these people love you.

00:07:50.702 --> 00:07:52.471
I can't --
I can't believe it."

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:54.407
That's her way
of complimenting me.

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:56.074
But I'll take it.
-That's kinda...

00:07:56.074 --> 00:07:58.210
There's a sweetness
somewhere in there.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:01.246
-She loves that people love me.
It's sweet.

00:08:01.246 --> 00:08:02.481
-And what about your dad?

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:04.950
-My dad is the sweetest,
so supportive.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.052
He went to my Netflix special
taping, which was a couple ago,

00:08:07.052 --> 00:08:08.620
and I kicked him out
during the middle of it

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:09.788
because it occurred to me

00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:11.056
that it might be
uncomfortable for him.

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:12.425
And it was the first time
that it occurred to me.

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:13.759
And he goes,
"It was the first time?"

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:15.828
And I said, "Yes, Dad,"
because I have to shut that off.

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:18.197
If you're at a show --
I would hate if I went to a show

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:19.932
and I saw Cardi B
and she was like,

00:08:19.932 --> 00:08:21.700
"Listen, you guys,
my dad's in the crowd tonight.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.169
I can't do 'WAP.'"

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:25.537
I would be like, "This is...

00:08:25.537 --> 00:08:27.039
This is the wrong show
I came to."

00:08:27.039 --> 00:08:28.740
So I don't hold back
if my dad's there.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.577
But he did not come
to this HBO special taping

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.478
because he told me
that oftentimes when he comes

00:08:33.478 --> 00:08:35.648
to my shows afterwards,
people come up to him

00:08:35.648 --> 00:08:37.583
and treat him like
he's at my funeral.

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.185
They're like,
"Are you okay, man?

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:42.154
Like, do you want us to bring
a casserole by later this week?"

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:43.923
Like, he really suffers a lot,

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:46.525
but they are so supportive
and I'm really lucky.

00:08:46.525 --> 00:08:48.460
-Second season of "FBoy Island."

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.329
Give a quick pitch
for those who haven't seen.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:54.033
-Okay, the quick pitch is I have
not met one person who says --

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:56.301
Everyone always says, "I don't
usually like reality shows,

00:08:56.301 --> 00:08:57.603
but I love this one."

00:08:57.603 --> 00:08:58.904
You don't have to
like reality shows.

00:08:58.904 --> 00:09:00.639
You can be one of these people
who thinks you're better

00:09:00.639 --> 00:09:02.007
than them, but you're not.

00:09:02.007 --> 00:09:03.843
This show is amazing.
It's addictive.

00:09:03.843 --> 00:09:06.645
It's called a tour de force
by "Vanity Fair."

00:09:06.645 --> 00:09:08.213
And it's funny. I'm hosting it.

00:09:08.213 --> 00:09:10.215
All the things
you do on your couch

00:09:10.215 --> 00:09:12.050
to make fun of these shows,
I'm doing it as the host,

